meta {
  name: List Meta Campaigns
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/campaigns?tenant_id={{tenantId}}&mapping_status=unmapped
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  Backs the three admin grids. `mapping_status` is optional — omit it for every
  campaign, or pass unmapped / suggested / confirmed for one grid.

  Each row carries lead_count: how many leads that campaign has actually
  brought in, across every branch. It is the column that makes the grid usable,
  since an ad account holds years of dead campaigns and "which of these matter"
  is answerable only by volume.

  Requires super_admin and an explicit ?tenant_id= — never the caller's own
  tenant, since platform staff administer a tenant other than their own.

  Regression checks:
    * as tenant A, no row from tenant B appears. The scoping is
      ext.meta_campaigns' admin_tenant_config_policy, not a WHERE clause —
      there is deliberately no literal tenant_id filter in the query, so this
      test actually exercises the policy.
    * a bogus tenant_id            -> 404 "Tenant not found", not an empty list
    * missing tenant_id            -> 422
    * caller below super_admin     -> 403
}
